---
import BaseLayout from '../layouts/BaseLayout.astro'
---

<BaseLayout
  description="About Fret Canvas: a visual fretboard tool for scales, chord tones, tuning workflows, and export-ready diagrams."
  title="About | Fret Canvas"
>
  <div class="mx-auto flex w-full max-w-[72rem] flex-1 pt-10">
    <article class="w-full rounded-[var(--md-shape-lg)] border border-[color:var(--md-sys-color-outline-variant)] bg-[color:var(--md-sys-color-surface-container)] p-6 shadow-[var(--md-elevation-1)] md:p-8">
      <h1 class="text-3xl font-semibold tracking-tight text-[color:var(--md-sys-color-on-surface)]">
        About Fret Canvas
      </h1>
      <p class="mt-4 max-w-[56rem] text-base leading-7 text-[color:var(--md-sys-color-on-surface-variant)]">
        Fret Canvas is a fretboard visualizer for guitar and other string instruments. It helps you
        map scales, chord tones, and alternate tunings, then export clean diagrams as PNG or SVG.
      </p>

      <section class="mt-8 grid gap-4 md:grid-cols-2">
        <div class="rounded-[var(--md-shape-md)] border border-[color:var(--md-sys-color-outline-variant)] bg-[color:var(--md-sys-color-surface-container-low)] p-5">
          <h2 class="text-base font-medium text-[color:var(--md-sys-color-on-surface)]">
            What it does
          </h2>
          <ul class="mt-3 list-disc space-y-2 pl-5 text-sm leading-6 text-[color:var(--md-sys-color-on-surface-variant)]">
            <li>Visualize scales and chord tones on the fretboard</li>
            <li>Work with custom tunings and saved presets</li>
            <li>Control export range and preview output</li>
            <li>Export diagrams as PNG or SVG for publishing</li>
          </ul>
        </div>

        <div class="rounded-[var(--md-shape-md)] border border-[color:var(--md-sys-color-outline-variant)] bg-[color:var(--md-sys-color-surface-container-low)] p-5">
          <h2 class="text-base font-medium text-[color:var(--md-sys-color-on-surface)]">
            Who it is for
          </h2>
          <p class="mt-3 text-sm leading-6 text-[color:var(--md-sys-color-on-surface-variant)]">
            Players, teachers, and content creators who want a clean way to inspect note layouts and
            generate fretboard diagrams without spending time in design tools.
          </p>
        </div>
      </section>
    </article>
  </div>
</BaseLayout>
